Why Is Demand Increasing
Steel Decarbonization: EAF technology provides steelmakers with a flexible production route using scrap and DRI while reducing reliance on coke-based ironmaking.
Growing Scrap and DRI Utilization: Increased availability and use of scrap, DRI, and HBI are encouraging investments in flexible electric steelmaking systems.
Automation and Digitalization: Automated charging, electrode regulation, process control, scrap preheating, and digital furnace systems are improving productivity and operational consistency.

Industry Watch: EAF Technology Advances Steel Decarbonization
Steel producers are increasingly evaluating EAF technology as part of lower-carbon production strategies. Modern systems combine high-power electrical equipment, oxygen and carbon injection, scrap preheating, automation, slag control, and digital process models to improve productivity and energy performance.

